---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/recart-vs-postscript';
const title = 'Recart vs Postscript for Shopify SMS: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Compare Recart and Postscript for Shopify SMS program ownership, managed service, campaign approvals, attribution and migration.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Recart only for cart recovery?",
    "answer": "No. Its current materials describe list growth, campaigns, automations and managed SMS service. Check the specific plan and proposal."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is managed service included on every Recart plan?",
    "answer": "Its managed-service page names Scale and Enterprise plans. Confirm current inclusions in the written offer rather than assuming every tier is identical."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should decide between Recart and Postscript?",
    "answer": "Compare the required SMS program, the people who will operate it, approval controls, reporting definitions and total quoted costs. No fixed revenue mix guarantees a winner."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#5d3a1d]">Recart vs Postscript</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Recart vs Postscript for Shopify SMS</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">This is a choice between SMS programs and operating arrangements, not recovery-only software versus a full marketing platform. Recart advertises list growth, campaigns, automations and managed service. Postscript advertises collection, segmentation and reply integrations. Compare who will run the program and how they will demonstrate its value.</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Recart is broader than cart recovery</h2>
        <p>Recart describes managed onboarding, custom email and SMS popups, core automations and recurring segmented campaigns. Its Shopify listing also describes list growth and campaign personalization. A historical association with Messenger or cart recovery should not define the current comparison. Require the current proposal to identify channels and deliverables; do not presume Messenger support or a recovery-only price model. Postscript similarly needs to be assessed against a complete program rather than a single cart flow.</p>
        <h2>Make service scope comparable</h2>
        <p>Ask Recart which plan includes the proposed managed work and what remains with the merchant. Its managed-service page names Scale and Enterprise plans. For Postscript, obtain the actual service arrangement being offered rather than assuming every account is entirely self-service or fully managed. List responsibility for popup design, segmentation, copy, scheduling, reporting and replies. A cheaper software quote can become a more expensive operating arrangement when it excludes work your store cannot staff.</p>
        <h2>Proposed campaign approval rehearsal</h2>
        <p>Use a hypothetical footwear release to evaluate the operating model. Give each candidate the same product brief, stock constraint, audience rule and creative approval process. Ask for a draft release campaign and an abandonment flow, then request a stock-driven revision before approval. This exercise has not been run and has no recorded timing result. Record who edits the audience, who checks the link and who authorizes the send. Managed execution is useful only if the merchant retains the appropriate approval and emergency pause controls.</p>
        <h2>Compare list growth without changing the offer</h2>
        <p>Both candidates should demonstrate the required collection surface. Keep placement, offer and audience consistent where possible, and inspect signup source, permission records and destination status. Include a mobile visitor and an existing subscriber returning to the site. Recart advertises custom popups as part of its service, while Postscript documents its own collection tools. Neither product should be dismissed as unable to grow a list merely because the evaluation started with cart reminders.</p>
        <h2>Separate reporting from incremental value</h2>
        <p>Build a worksheet with campaign and automation sends, text costs, attributed orders, refunds and opt-outs. Document each vendor attribution rule before comparing dashboards. Recart advertises click-only attribution, but a click attribution setting still does not prove that all credited orders were caused by SMS. Ask how a proposed holdout would exclude other messaging differences and how much uncertainty remains. Do not move promotional SMS to email solely to lower a bill without considering whether the audience and purpose remain served.</p>
        <h2>Inspect replies, exclusions and cutover</h2>
        <p>Demonstrate a purchase before a reminder, a subscriber opt-out, an unavailable product and a product-question reply. Postscript advertises help-desk integrations; Recart service scope should specify who handles replies and escalation. For migration, inventory exportable status and permission records before importing. Assign one active SMS sender during each cutover step. A parallel account setup does not require parallel promotional sending. Agree on rollback triggers based on missing records or incorrect messages rather than promising a revenue-neutral migration.</p>
        <h2>Price the whole program and choose its owner</h2>
        <p>Request a normal-period and sale-period estimate using identical message assumptions, recipient countries and creative. Include plan fees, usage, service deliverables, approval labor and contract terms. Keep email costs visible if that platform remains. Choose Recart when the demonstrated managed arrangement solves the staffing gap; choose Postscript when its demonstrated tools and service arrangement fit the team. These are conditional fit criteria, not measured rankings. Neither broadcast revenue share nor a fixed subscriber count can decide the platform without examining work and cost.</p>
        <h2>Primary sources and evaluation limits</h2>
        <p>Reviewed 25 November 2026. These sources establish advertised scope, not measured results or account-specific behavior. Product exercises above are proposed and unrun; plan availability, quotes and store configuration require confirmation.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://recart.com/fully-managed-sms">Recart managed service</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/recart">Recart Shopify listing</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/features">Postscript collection and reply tools</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-sendlane">Postscript vs Sendlane</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Klaviyo vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-attentive">Postscript vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/beauty">Email apps for beauty stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Recart vs Postscript FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
